**Chain of causation:** r6 has no `ospfd` process and no OSPF configuration whatsoever. r7's sole OSPF link is `eth0` (67.1.1.2/8) toward r6 on the Y collision domain. With r6 not participating in OSPF, r7 cannot form any adjacency, so its routes — `17.x.x.x` loopbacks, `67.0.0.0/8` (the R6–R7 link), `70.0.0.0/8` (R7's LAN) — are never flooded into area 0.0.0.1 and never reach R1. The team's assumption that R7 failed is incorrect; R7's FRR stack is fully healthy.

